#import "../lib.typ": *

#part("II", "Thinking in Lists")

#part-intro[
  Part I used lists as boxes of things. Part II opens the box. You'll see what a list is made of, then learn the two ways Lisp programmers work through lists: recursion, and functions that take other functions. By the end of Part II, lists will feel like the natural shape for almost any data.
  
]
